Python {{ python_version }}+, uv, Ruff, strict mypy, pytest, and prek. Application
code lives in `src/{{ project_slug }}/`; tests import the installed package.

## Setup

Install the uv version required by `uv.toml` using your usual uv installer.
For a newly generated project:

```bash
git init
uv lock
uv run --locked poe setup
```

Commit `uv.lock` with the project. It belongs to this project, not the template.
For an existing checkout, run `uv run --locked poe setup` using the committed lock.
`uv.toml`, the dev dependency, and Docker's uv version are updated together.

Run the application:

```bash
uv run --locked python -m {{ project_slug }}
```

## Development

Use `uv run --locked poe <task>`:

| Task | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `lint` | Apply Ruff lint fixes |
| `format` | Format code |
| `check` | Strict mypy checks over source and tests |
| `test` | Fast pytest run |
| `test-cov` | Tests with branch coverage and an XML report |
| `flc` | Fix lint, format, and check types |
| `flct` | Fix lint, format, check types, and test |
| `validate` | Read-only lint/format checks, type checking, and coverage tests |
| `sync` | Install committed dependency versions |
| `install-hooks` | Install prek commit hooks |

Prek runs Ruff on changed files and mypy over the project. The conventional
`.pre-commit-config.yaml` format is retained. Run all hooks with
`uv run --locked prek run --all-files`. CI uses `validate`, so it rejects code
that needs fixing. `uv add`, `uv remove`, and deliberate dependency upgrades are
expected to update the lockfile; commit those changes together.

Coverage reports include branches. Choose a coverage floor for your project's
behavior instead of inheriting an arbitrary template percentage. Add specific
coverage exclusions through `exclude_also` to preserve coverage.py's defaults.

## Dependency updates

Enable the Renovate GitHub App for this repository. `renovate.json` configures
updates for dependencies, Actions, hooks, and Docker where present, plus lockfile
maintenance. The uv configuration, dependency, and Docker image version should
move together. Review updates and require successful validation before merging.
