## CI and template updates

PR validation checks formatting, lint, types, and tests against `uv.lock`.
The manual **Update from template** workflow updates the template, refreshes the
project lockfile, and validates before opening a PR. Its PR body links to the
successful validation run. PRs opened with `GITHUB_TOKEN` do not automatically
trigger the ordinary PR checks; edits made afterward need fresh validation.
Repositories requiring those PR checks can use a separately configured GitHub
App token for PR creation. Enable GitHub Actions' permission to create PRs in
the repository settings before using the update workflow.
{% endif %}

## Updating older projects

When adopting the `src/` layout, merge your existing application modules into
`src/{{ project_slug }}/` and resolve Copier conflicts before validating. Remove
the obsolete top-level package only after preserving its local changes. Update
custom imports, build steps, and Docker asset copies that refer to the old path.
Run `uv lock`, `uv sync --locked`, and `uv run --locked poe validate`, then check
your application entry point. Replace old pre-commit hooks with
`uv run --locked prek install`.
